  "description": "RECORDED TODAY-BEHAVIOUR, DELIBERATELY DIVERGENT IN THE PLAN. Re-presenting the SAME claim triple currently returns null because start() only matches queued requests. Plan §2.5 marks this [Δ]: chiefd must return the already-claimed request so `null` can mean 'no work AND you hold nothing'. This fixture pins what the TypeScript does so the divergence is explicit and reviewable rather than discovered during the port.",
